519997e7 (666 1793268076626 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f376") (src . "code-suggest: a comment no longer ends the statement it follows\n\nThe table scan (every language but JavaScript and TypeScript) decided\nwhether a line continues the statement before it from the line's last\ntoken, and a block comment counted as that token: `var z = 1 + /* note */`\nread as finished, so a definition-looking line after it could be taken as\na strict cut although the statement goes on. A line holding only a\ncomment, or lying inside one, also reset the judgement, so `x = 1 +`, then\n`// note`, then such a line, was taken too. A comment's text is never\ncode now: what a line continues with is its last code before a comment,\nand a line with no code (blank, a comment only, inside a block comment)\nleaves the statement as the line before it did. A complete statement\nfollowed by a comment, or a comment alone after one, still ends there.\n\n- code-suggest.sc: the table scan's last code ignores comments; a line\n  without code keeps the previous line's judgement.\n- README: the --symbols paragraph says so.\n- Tests: import-symbols (an operator then a block comment in Go, Rust, C\n  and Java; a comment closing on the next line; a comment-only line after\n  an operator in Go, C and shell; controls after complete statements);\n  rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 508))))
